    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154798,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours most commonly arise in subcutaneous tissue of the trunk or proximal extremities, with a smaller subset presenting in the head and neck {31008539; 34272753; 37338620; 35583270; 39887195; 34647172; 38986510; 40159029}. Rare dermal and intramuscular cases have been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154799,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients report a slow-growing mass with a preoperative duration ranging from weeks to years. Tumour size is typically &lt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;mm, although reported cases reach up to 158&nbsp;mm. The tumours may be painful or pigmented {35583270; 37338620}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154800,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>PRRX1</em>-rearranged fibroblastic tumours are rare with less than 30&nbsp;cases in the literature, although this probably represents an underestimate {31008539; 34272753; 37338620; 35583270; 39887195; 34647172; 38986510; 40159029}. These tumours present over a wide age range with a median in the fourth decade of life {41036703}. To date, one paediatric tumour has been reported {40958368}. Female individuals are more commonly affected than male individuals, with an M:F&nbsp;ratio of 1.5:1 {41036703}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154801,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154802,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The vast majority of tumours are characterized by <em>PRRX1</em> fusions to <em>NCOA1</em>. The <em>PRRX1</em> breakpoint is consistently located at exon&nbsp;1, while the <em>NCOA1</em> breakpoint is located at exon&nbsp;13 or (less often) exon&nbsp;15 {31008539; 34272753; 38986510}. Less common partners of <em>PRRX1</em> include <em>NCOA2</em> and <em>KMT2D</em> {31913156; 37338620; 40159029}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154803,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Grossly, tumours present as a circumscribed, tan-white, firm to rubbery mass ranging from 20&nbsp;to 160&nbsp;mm (median: 40&nbsp;mm).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154804,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours present as a circumscribed, occasionally multilobular mass with elongated, irregular, and ectatic vascular spaces evident at low magnification. Closer inspection shows a predominantly paucicellular neoplasm composed of bland spindle cells arranged haphazardly or in short fascicles within a hyalinized background. Focal increased cellularity, myxoid/oedematous stromal change, or dense eosinophilic ropy or wire-like collagen are often appreciated. Tumours with <em>KMT2D</em> alterations appear to have especially prominent perivascular hyalinization, and a subset of superficial cases may show scattered clusters of pigmented dendritic cells {37338620; 31913156; 35583270}. The tumour cells have monomorphic ovoid nuclei with small nucleoli and scant pale cytoplasm with tapering processes. Mitotic activity is inconspicuous, at &lt;&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (equating to &lt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;mitosis/10&nbsp;HPF measuring 0.5&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> in area), and necrosis is absent.</p>\r\n<p>By immunohistochemistry, the tumour cells may show patchy staining for S100 and/or SOX10 but are usually negative for SMA, desmin, CD34, STAT6, MUC4, and estrogen receptor {31008539; 34272753; 37338620; 35583270; 39887195; 34647172; 38986510; 40159029}. Pigmented cases may express melanocytic markers {35583270}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154805,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154806,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Identification of a <em>PRRX1</em> rearrangement helps differentiate this tumour from other fibroblastic neoplasms.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1134,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154807,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a paucicellular, circumscribed, bland spindle cell neoplasm; hyalinized stroma with variably wire-like and ropy collagen; prominent ectatic and irregular vascular spaces; demonstration of <em>PRRX1</em> rearrangement.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1132,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154808,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1133,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154809,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although follow-up data are limited, this tumour type appears to be benign {31008539; 34647172; 37338620}. To date, no local recurrences or distant metastases have been reported following conservative excision, with follow-up in some studies approaching 2&nbsp;years.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]